-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",437,{
[13953]="7004E1E3\n1\tDwarves can be found throughout Erebor. King Thorin has asked you to question the Dwarves of Erebor regarding rumours he has heard of a new expedition forming against his will to reclaim Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep.\t\n2\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have questioned many dwarves of Erebor concerning rumours of a forbidden expedition to Thikil-gundu. You should inform King Thorin III of what you learned.\n3\tTalk to Dori outside Erebor\tDori can be found somewhere outside Erebor. King Thorin III has asked you to speak to Dori and learn what he knows of the rumoured expedition to Thikil-gundu.\n4\tFind Nori\tNori can be found within the eastern keep outside Erebor. Dori has asked you to speak to Nori regarding unusual visitors to the coffers of Erebor.\n5\tCollect Nori's missive\tNori's missive is pinned to the door of one of the eastern keeps of Erebor. You have not found Nori, but you discovered a missive pinned to the door of the eastern keep. You should take it.\n6\tRead Nori's missive\tYou have taken Nori's missive and should now read it.\n7\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have discovered that Nori and a small company of dwarves set out for the Grey Mountains against the will of King Thorin III. You should inform King Thorin of what has happened.\n",
[13954]="70059351\n1\tFind the ruffians' camp-site\tThe ruffians' camp-site can be found north of Trader's Wharf. You should find the ruffians' camp-site on the shores of the Wildwood.\n2\tThe ruffians' camp-site can be found north of Trader's Wharf. You should destroy the ruffians' camp-site.\t\n3\tDestroy the ruffians' camp-fire\030Wait for someone to return\tThe ruffians' camp-site can be found north of Trader's Wharf. You should destroy the ruffians' camp-site.\n4\tInterrogate the tomb-robber\tThe ruffians' camp-site can be found north of Trader's Wharf. You should talk to the tomb-robber at the ruffians' camp-site.\n5\tDefeat hardened tomb-robbers in the Wildwood (total: 8)\tHardened tomb-robbers are wandering in the Wildwood. You should defeat any hardened tomb-robbers that you find in the Wildwood.\n6\tFind the tomb-robbers' camp-site in the Wildwood\tThe tomb-robbers' camp-site can be found in the Wildwood. You should find the tomb-robbers' camp-site.\n7\tSummon the lead tomb-robber\030Defeat the lead tomb-robber\tThe tomb-robbers' camp-site can be found in the Wildwood. You should summon and defeat the lead tomb-robber.\n8\tInterrogate the lead tomb-robber\tThe tomb-robber camp-site can be found in the Wildwood. You should talk to the lead tomb-robber.\n9\tTalk to Enid Nettlesting\tEnid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should talk to Enid Nettlesting.\n",
[13955]="7000A2AB\n1\tDefeat tomb-robber captain at Cirith Rhîw\tThe captain of a robber-band maintains control of the road leading to the gate at Cirith Rhîw, north of Ost Forod. Spring Standish has asked you to defeat a tomb-robber captain at Cirith Rhîw, in hopes that the rest of his band will disperse.\n2\tTalk to Spring Standish\tSpring Standish is at Ost Forod, the old watch-post in the hills of Tyrn Fornech, south of Cirith Rhîw. You have defeated the tomb-robber captain at Cirith Rhîw and should return to Spring with news of your victory.\n",
[13956]="70019319\n1\tEarn Helhathel's favour\030Earn Glavrolnen's favour\tGlavrolnen and Helhathel are at the Elf-camp in Nen Hilith. Ovorlas is pleased at your arrival and has set you to earning the favour of his assistants, Glavrolnen and Helhathel, in the vale of Nen Hilith.\n2\tTalk to Ovorlas at Nen Hilith\tOvorlas is at the Elf-camp in Nen Hilith. Now that you have earned the favour of Glavrolnen and Helhathel, you should return to Ovorlas.\n",
[13957]="7000D5B7\n1\tTalk to Frideric the Elder\tSpeak with Frideric in Ost Guruth to arrange a fast mount to Trestlebridge. WARNING: Completing this quest will immediately send you to Trestlebridge in the North Downs.\n",
[13958]="70002E13\n1\tTalk to Alphlanc\tAlphlanc is at the Last Bridge on the western edge of the Trollshaws, where the road passes into the Lone-lands. Barachen has asked you to speak again with Alphlanc at the Last Bridge to see if she has learned anything of the missing dwarves.\n2\tSearch the area around the Last Bridge\tThe Last Bridge supports the road as it winds west out of the Trollshaws and passes into the Lone-lands. Alphlanc has asked you to search the area immediately around the Last Bridge closely for some sign of the missing dwarves.\n3\tSearch the shattered dwarf-crate\tA smashed crate lies at the foot of the Last Bridge, on the water's edge. You have located a smashed crate by the Last Bridge that appears to be of dwarf-make. You should investigate further.\n4\tTalk to Alphlanc\tAlphlanc is at the Last Bridge on the western edge of the Trollshaws, where the road passes into the Lone-lands. You should tell Alphlanc what you have found.\n5\tTalk to Heithur Ironfist\tHeithur Ironfist is at Barachen's camp, east of the Last Bridge, on a sloping hill in the shadow of the southern cliffs. Alphlanc believes that Heithur will want to hear about your discovery of a shattered dwarf-crate at the base of the Last Bridge, emptied of its contents, for it means that Heithur's company met with an unfortunate fate.\n",
[13959]="7006895A\n1\tDefeat Heirsworn at Dâr Jeraf and Kamîr Kateb (total: 8)\tShûba has asked you to defeat a number of Heirsworn. Heirsworn can be found in the ruined area of the Tor-gardens, to the north-west.\n2\tTalk to Shûba at the Pot and Quill\tYou have defeated a number of Heirsworn. You should report back to Shûba at the Pot and Quill.\n",
[13960]="70000170\n1\tSpeak with Celandine Brandybuck at Newbury in Buckland\tThe propery of Newbury is in Buckland. Follow the road west from Bree until you see the Brandywine Bridge, then turn south into Buckland. Talk to Celandine Brandybuck at Newbury in Buckland.\n",
[13961]="70009A5A\n1\tEnsure Pearlina Gamgee's home is safe\tPearlina Gamgee's residence is located in Dwaling, east of Hob Hillbrow's home. Hob Hillbrow asked you to check on the home of one his friends, Pearlina Gamgee.\n2\tDefeat the Chief's watcher\tRemove the ruffians living on Pearlina Gamgee's property. Hob Hillbrow asked you to check on the home of one his friends, Pearlina Gamgee.\n3\tTalk to Hob Hillbrow in the Bullroarer's Sward\tHob Hillbrow is at his home at the Bullroarer's Sward in Dwaling, west of Pearlina Gamgee's property. You were attacked by ruffians outside Pearlina Gamgee's residence. You should inform Hob Hillbrow.\n",
[13962]="7001A771\n1\tFree the southern hillside\030Free the western hillside\030Free Hyacinth's entranceway\tThe first step to breaking the siege on the Great Smials is to reclaim the south and west sides of the hill.\n2\tFree the eastern hillside\030Free Edilina's entranceway\tWith the south and west sides in your control, it is now time to break the enemy's hold on the eastern hillside.\n3\tFree the courtyard of the Great Smials\tThe hillsides have been claimed for the Free Peoples. Now the courtyard has opened and may be assaulted.\n4\tDefeat the half-orc at the doorway to the Great Smials and claim the Great Smials\tThe courtyard has fallen. Now all that remains is to defeat the leader of the assault and break the siege.\n",
[13963]="70029FBF\n1\tComplete 'Trouble in Tuckborough' in a raid group\tTuckborough is the chief village of Tookland and home to the Thain of the Shire. Goblins and half-orcs seek to capture it in the name of Sharkey, the brigand chieftain troubling Bree-land and the Shire.\n",
[13964]="70022D37\n1\tTalk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs\tThe ranger camp is located south and slightly west of Harndirion in the Lich Bluffs. Find Mincham and speak to him of the curse upon the lichbluffs.\n",
[13965]="70052B19\n1\tFind the missing woodsmen and learn what happened at Tríubad\tTríubad can be found by travelling eastward from Hultvís and following the footpath into the hills of Woodsedge. Ríkmar has asked you to find missing woodsmen and learn what has been slowing their efforts to rebuild Hultvís. Ríkmar believes the missing woodsmen can likely be found somewhere near Tríubad.\n2\tTalk to Clothar\tClothar can be found along the footpath to the south-east of Hultvís. You have discovered two of the woodsmen of Hultvís and their damaged cart along the road to Tríubad. You should ask them what has happened.\n3\tCollect seasoned lumber (total: 8)\030Collect tanned hides (total: 6)\tSeasoned lumber and tanned hides can be found at Tríubad. Clothar and Vilibald have asked for your help in recovering the resources they were forced to leave behind when they fled Tríubad.\n4\tFind Clothar's axe and defeat the tree-demon of Tríubad\tClothar's axe can be found somewhere near the pond at Tríubad. Clothar claims that his axe was stolen by an angry tree-demon and has begged you to retrieve it.\n5\tDeliver the lumber, hides, and axe to Clothar on the road to Tríubad\tClothar can be found along the road to Tríubad. You have recovered the lumber and hides Clothar and his kinsmen were forced to abandon at Tríubad, and you have also recovered Clothar's family axe. You should return to Clothar.\n6\tTalk to Ríkmar\tRíkmar can be found in Hultvís. You have aided the woodsmen of Tríubad in repelling the Taurogrim and recovering their lost resources. You should return to Ríkmar with these good tidings.\n",
[13966]="7002EF0F\n1\tFind the Orc that has Sperling's sword\t\n2\tFind the Orc that has Sperling's sword\tMounted Orcs can be found throughout the Entwash Vale. Tracks move away to the east. You should hunt mounted Orcs until you find the one that has Sperling's sword.\n",
[13967]="7002FCEF\n1\tTalk to Gísling\tGísil, Thane of Garsfeld, wishes you to speak to his son, Gísling, about the troubles Garsfeld is facing. Gísling is inside the mead-hall in Garsfeld.\n2\tTalk to Gísil\tHaving spoken to Gísling about the troubles facing Garsfeld, you should return to Gísil. Gísil is inside the mead-hall of Garsfeld.\n",
[13968]="7002EF27\n1\tTrack paw-prints\t\n2\tTrack paw-prints\tThere are paw-prints leading away from the place where you found Sperling's sword. You should track the dog that stole Sperling's sword.\n3\tTrack the paw-prints\tThere are paw-prints leading south, away from the place where you found Sperling's sword. You should track the dog that stole Sperling's sword.\n4\tTrack the paw-prints\tThere are paw-prints leading south, away from the place where you found Sperling's sword. You should track the dog that stole Sperling's sword.\n5\tTrack the paw-prints\tThere are paw-prints leading south-east, away from the place where you found Sperling's sword. You should track the dog that stole Sperling's sword.\n6\tTrack the paw-prints\tThere are paw-prints leading south-east, away from the place where you found Sperling's sword. You should track the dog that stole Sperling's sword.\n7\tTrack the paw-prints\tThere are paw-prints leading south-east, away from the place where you found Sperling's sword. You should track the dog that stole Sperling's sword.\n",
[13969]="7002F90B\n1\tTravel towards the farmhouses and search for any in need of aid\tThe farmhouses in peril are south-west of the trader's outpost. Ofrith has asked you to carefully search among the farmhouses to the west for signs of any remaining farmers who may be in danger.\n2\tTalk to the frightened man\tThe farmhouses in peril are south-west of the trader's outpost. You have discovered a man at one of the large farmhouse estates who seems to be in need of your aid.\n",
[13970]="7002EE65\n1\tAccompany Getfleda to help break up a fight between her friends\tGetfleda is in the northern part of Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale. Getfleda asked you to help break up a fight between her friends Brunstan and Sperling. You should speak with her again when you are ready to leave.\n2\tTalk to Getfleda in Eaworth\tGetfleda is in the northern part of Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale. You should speak with Getfleda regarding the dispute between her friends Brunstan and Sperling.\n",
[13971]="7004DA21\n1\tDefeat Taurogrim in Eryn Lasgalen (total: 10)\tTaurogrim can be found in Eryn Lasgalen. You should defeat Taurogrim in Eryn Lasgalen.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Taurogrim in Eryn Lasgalen.\n",
[13972]="700108F8\n1\tThere are many folks in Bree-town who might be interested in participating in your game of Troves and Trickery. Bryony Elmwood has challenged you to a game of Troves and Trickery. You should speak to several townspeople and perform tricks for their amusement. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n2\tTalk to Bryony Elmwood at the Bree Festival Grounds\tBryony Elmwood is at the Festival Grounds in Bree. You should return to Bryony Elmwood with word of your successes at Troves and Trickery.\n",
[13973]="700108FA\n1\tThere are many Elves in Duillond who might like to participate in your game of Troves and Trickery. Gloreniel has challenged you to a game of Troves and Trickery. You should speak to several Elves and perform tricks for their amusement. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n2\tTalk to Gloreniel\tGloreniel is at the Duillond Festival Grounds. You should return to Gloreniel with word of your successes in Troves and Trickery.\n",
[13974]="700108FB\n1\tUse whistle near Townperson\tThere are many dwarves throughout Thorin's Hall who might enjoy a game of Troves and Trickery. Guthlág has challenged you to participate in a game of Troves and Trickery. You should speak to several dwarves and perform tricks for their amusement. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Guthlág in Thorin's Hall\tGuthlág is in the Inn at Thorin's Hall. You should return to Guthlág with word of your successes in Troves and trickery.\n",
[13975]="700108F9\n1\tThere are many hobbits throughout the Hobbiton-Bywater area who enjoy the challenge of Troves and Trickery. Egbert Took has challenged you to a game of troves and trickery. You should speak to several hobbits and perform tricks for their amusement. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n2\tTalk to Egbert Took\tEgbert Took is at the Party Tree. You should return to Egbert Took with word of your successes at Troves and Trickery.\n",
[13976]="70041044\n1\tBring the poem to Barían\tBarían can be found in the Masons' Quarter in Dol Amroth. You should bring Rhovendol's poem to Barían.\n2\tFind Barían's stonework in its wheelbarrow\tBarían's sample of stonework can be found in a wheelbarrow in the Scholar's Quarter. You should lift the stonework and carry it to Master Laegened, so that he can see Barían's artistry, and see if she is worthy of an apprenticeship.\n3\tSpeak with Laegened\tLaegened is in the Mason's Quarter in Dol Amroth. You should speak with Laegened.\n4\tSpeak with Barían\tBarían can be found in the Mason's Quarter in Dol Amroth. You should tell Barían the good news.\n5\tTell Rhovendol that Barían has no interest in him\tRhovendol is in the Scholar's Quarter of Dol Amroth. You should tell Rhovendol that Barían is not interested in him.\n",
[13977]="7004E92F\n1\tFind old crafting tools\tFind old crafting tools.\n2\tFind old crafting tools (total: 8)\tYou should search for old crafting tools in Stormwall.\n3\tBring the crafting tools to Hórin\tYou should bring the crafting tools to Hórin in Skarháld.\n",
[13978]="700593C0\n1\tRecover stolen supplies (total: 10)\030Defeat Wildwood assailants (total: 8)\030Defeat the waggon snatcher\tThe brigands and their leader took off up the road east of Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood. You should follow the trail of stolen supplies and deal with any brigands along the way.\n2\tTalk to Minda Heathertoes\tMinda is on a hill near her broken waggon, in the eastern Wildwood. You should talk to Minda Heathertoes.\n",
[13979]="70018E1D\n1\tDefeat intruders within Tumun-ghâr (total: 20)\tThe entrance to Tumun-ghâr lies within Gharâaf-fehem. Alwar has asked you to assist him in clearing Tumun-ghâr of the vermin within.\n2\tTalk to Alwar at Gharâf-fehem\tAlwar can be found at Gharâf-fehem in the Redhorn Lodes. You should return to Alwar to receive a reward for your efforts.\n",
[13980]="70018E1C\n1\tDefeat the leader of the intruders in Tumun-ghâr\tThe entrance to Tumun-ghâr lies within Gharâf-fehem. Alwar has asked you to defeat the leader of the intruders within Tumun-ghâr.\n2\tTalk to Alwar at Gharâf-fehem\tAlwar is at Gharâf-fehem. You should return to Alwar with news of your success.\n",
[13981]="70018E1F\n1\tBring the miner's tool-kits to Alwar at Gharâf-fehem in the Redhorn Lodes\030Collect miner's tool-kits (total: 8)\tThe entrance to Tumun-ghâr lies within Gharâf-fehem. Alwar has asked you to collect Miner's Tool-kits from within Tumun-ghâr.\n",
[13982]="7000178A\n1\tTravel to the cross-roads north along the Greenway\tThe Greenway heads north from Trestlebridge to a cross-roads, where it continues north or turns east. Aggy Digweed has suggested that you turn east at the cross-roads.\n2\tInvestigate the camp-fire at the edge of the darkened fields\tThe camp-fire can be found north-west of the cross-roads in the North Downs. You should find the source of the fire's light.\n",
[13983]="70053F4C\n1\tEasterling defectors can be found in Parth Daenath. You should attempt to convince the Easterling defectors to turn on the Enemy.\t\n2\tTalk to Huneric\tHuneric can be found at Adambel. You should talk to Huneric.\n",
[13984]="7004BEB3\n1\tYou should bribe the poor in Fushaum Bal North.\t\n2\tTalk to the Haradrim Commander\tThe Haradrim Commander can be found at Fushaum Bal South. You should talk to the Haradrim Commander.\n",
})
